 past sell-offs it fell 61% in the 2020 crash, 51% in the 2022 bear market and 86% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $15.50 (margin of safety -282%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 10%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $9.12 to $25.96 (P10-P90).","On multiples it looks expensive against Basic Materials peers: P/E 24.9 vs 16.3, EV/EBITDA 10.6 vs 8.3 and P/FCF 76.2 vs 22.4 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 68% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 1.3% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 6.2% (vs the 8% bar).","The 22 covering analysts target $78.22 on average, 32% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 21% clears the cost of capital of 10.2% by 11pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.27).","It converts 4% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 2.55x.","ROE of 12% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (3.1x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 16pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 0.5% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 0.6x net debt to EBITDA ($3.8B of cash against $9.4B of debt), with interest covered 25.5x.","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.29)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 4.3% over 3 years, 12.8% over 5 years and 5.0% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 22%).","At current returns, reinvesting 52% of profits supports about 11.2% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 1.1% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 62%.","Capex runs 2.0x depreciation (17.3% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 17, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.7%), and institutions hold 90%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (5 sales, net $8.4M sold).","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.1% (0.1% in buybacks and 1.0% in dividends)."],"people":["With about 29,000 employees, each generates about $894K of revenue, 1.4x the Basic Materials median.","That works out to $38K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.0M (3x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Culture flags: recent layoff news.","Stock compensation averages $4K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":61,"head":"Avoid: priced 282% above its fair value of $15.50.","pros":["Composite 47, above the 39 line (gates 12/26)","ROIC 21.4% vs WACC 10.2%","Revenue grew 12.8%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 0.6x","22 analysts' mean target $78.22 (+32%)"],"cons":["Trades 282% above fair value of $15.50","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","P/E 24.9x vs sector 16.3x","EV/EBITDA 10.6x vs sector 8.3x","P/FCF 76.2x vs sector 22.4x"],"flags":["Priced 282% above its fair value of $15.50"],"need":[],"buy_below":13.17,"vc":{"base":15.5,"base_src":"dcf","bear":9.12,"bull":25.96,"alt_median":12.78,"n_alt":3,"gap":0.2131,"dispersion":0.1009,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide"]},"med":{"pe":16.2619,"ev_ebitda":8.35,"pfcf":22.4216,"pb":2.0723,"roic":0.0575,"gross_margin":0.2532,"fcf_margin":0.052,"div_yield":0.0194}},"mc_quantiles":[5.72,7.7,9.12,10.26,11.11,11.91,12.71,13.45,14.27,15.0,15.73,16.69,17.48,18.31,19.35,20.68,22.12,23.47,25.96,28.99,38.24],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.493,"discount_rate":0.228,"terminal_growth":0.013,"exit_multiple":0.266},"ticker":"FCX","date":"2026-11-13"}